## Breaking and Building Strings

Split a string into parts by a delimiter, and join a collection back into a single string.

### str_split — Break Apart

```xiom
let csv = "apple,banana,cherry";
let parts = str_split(csv, ",");  // ["apple", "banana", "cherry"]

let sentence = "Hello World XIOM";
let words = str_split(sentence, " ");  // ["Hello", "World", "XIOM"]
```

### Processing Split Results

```xiom
let line = "Alice:95:active";
let fields = str_split(line, ":");
// fields: ["Alice", "95", "active"]

let name = fields[0];
let score = fields[1];
let status = fields[2];
```

### join — Combine Back

```xiom
let words = Vec[Str]();
words.push("Hello");
words.push("World");
words.push("XIOM");

let sentence = join(words, " ");  // "Hello World XIOM"
let csv = join(words, ",");        // "Hello,World,XIOM"
```

### Practical Patterns

```xiom
// Parse key-value pairs
fn parse_config(line: Str) -> (Str, Str) {
  let parts = str_split(line, "=");
  if parts.len() >= 2 {
    return (parts[0], parts[1]);
  }
  return (line, "");
}

// Count words
fn word_count(text: Str) -> Int {
  let words = str_split(text, " ");
  return words.len();
}

// Build path from segments
fn build_path(segments: Vec[Str]) -> Str {
  return join(segments, "/");
}
```

### Split on Multiple Lines

```xiom
let text = "line1
line2
line3";
let lines = str_split(text, "
");
```

